Dear S people,

I would like to ask you the following:

Let's suppose that I have a n*p matrix of p binary variables
(n=number of observations) and a k*p matrix of probabilities. I
want to compute the following matrix:

X <- matrix(sample(rep(0:1, 500*8)), 500, 8)
p <- matrix(sample(rep(seq(0.11,0.9,.01), 100)), 100, 8)
########
#S-PLUS 2000 for Windows Release 1
resources({
g <- matrix(0, nrow=nrow(X), ncol=nrow(p))
for(i in 1:nrow(X)){
g[i, ] <- apply(p, 1, function(p, X, i) prod(ifelse(X[i,]==1, p,
1-p)), X, i)
}
})
 CPU Elasped % CPU Child Cache Working 
  NA  191 sec   NA     0     0  632036

As the number of observations n increases the procedure becomes
very slow. Is there any other more efficient way to do this?

Thanks in advance for your suggestions,
Dimitris

