On Thu, 5 Dec 2002, Trudi O'Farrell wrote:

> I am operating on Windows95 using Splus v6.1
>
> I have been using S-Plus for about 12 months and I recently have needed to 
> look into using the R program because I need to utilise a "package" developed 
> under R.
>
> Unfortunately I have little knowledge of R and would prefer to continue using 
> S-Plus to use these new "packages". What I would like to know is, is it 
> possible to take the R-Package (saved as a zip file) and some how attach as a 
> library in S-Plus and access the 'package" components through S-Plus?  a). 
> Will this work, or is it possible? b). What method do I use to attach and use 
> the R files?

You might do better to ask on R-help.  Since you mention zip files, I
think you have been looking at pre-compiled packages for Windows. You
cannot use those on S-PLUS without picking them apart, and probably not at
all if compiled code is involved.  You can port the sources (.tar.gz
files), provided you have the appropriate tools (including a C or Fortran
compiler as needed).  You might get to appreciate the effort that goes
into providing pre-compiled packages for Windows users of both S-PLUS and
R, as it can be a tricky process.

