Many thanks to Luciano Molinari, John Fox, Patrick Burns, Bert Gunther, James 
Holtman and Brian Ripley,

My query was: how do I get the mode of objects whose names are returned by 
objects()?
(Original post attached below.)

I modified LM's suggestion to:

> sapply(objects(), function(txt) mode(get(txt))) 

which was also proposed by PB, BG, JH and BR. JF suggested

> sapply(objects(), function(x) mode(eval(parse(text=x))))

Which makes me ponder the difference between get(x) and eval(parse(x)) when x 
is a string containing a variable name.  The following give the same answer 
(apart from the first component, which is the mode of .Last.value):

> sapply(objects(where=2), function(x) mode(get(x, where=2))) 
> sapply(objects(where=2), function(x) mode(eval(parse(text=x), local=2)))

(but probably not in all situations)

The first solution also seems to be about four times faster (from a small 
sample of evaluations on S+ 6.1 for Windows, NT4).

Rgds,

Robert

