Dear Guna,

At 06:15 AM 12/8/2002 -0800, sriram sampath wrote:
> hi,
>      am a student pursuing graduation in statistics,
> interested in the partial correlation between two
> variables suppressing more than one variable. I have
> gone thru many journals and books, but i could find
> only the algorithm suppressing one variable, pls help
> me in letting me know the algorithm(suppressing more
> than one variable Rxy.z1,z2,z3) for higher orders.

Here's a simple function to calculate the partial correlations between each 
pair of several variables controlling for the others; the argument R is the 
correlation matrix among the variables:

partials <- function(R){
    Rinv <- solve(R)
    D <- diag(sqrt(1/diag(Rinv)))
    - D %*% Rinv %*% D
    }

I hope that this helps,
 John

