Dear All,

Many thanks to all of you who have responded to my questions on
simulations. 

For those of you who are interested in running your simulation faster, I
would recommend you to first go through your functions and check the
time for each of your statement. You can use dos.time() or unix.time()
(depends on your operating sys!). Typically you would probably time your
statement inside your function using the inspect() command.
Alternatively Patrick Burns (http://www.burns-stat.com/)in his S poetry
site has a interlude command and James Holtman
(james.holtman at convergys.com) has some customized functions which will
check the time of your statements. 

