From Bill.Venables at CMIS.CSIRO.AU  Wed Dec 11 08:51:59 2002
From: Bill.Venables at CMIS.CSIRO.AU
Date: Wed, 11 Dec 2002 18:51:59 +1000
Subject: Re: Type I and III sum of squares
Message-ID: <E09E527B56BE2D438A3D6A246DDD27A9165719@roper-cv.qld.cmis.CSIRO.AU>

I 
think you have put your finger on one of the main problems with Type III sums of 
squares.  What you are asking for (additivity and order invariance) is 
not possible for a non-orthogonal design.  Type III sums of squares 
encourage people to think about their analyses in the wrong way: what they 
actually do is obscure precisely what hypothesis is being tested.  Get this 
straight and all is simplicity and light.

 

End 
of sermon.

 

Bill Venables.

