Dear S+ users,

I am struggling with how contrasts can be calculated in S+. For the sake of
simplicity, I will take a short example. 

Suppose a dataset X containing factor variables "A", "B", "C" and a
numerical response "R". If I use an analysis of variance : lm.result <- lm(R
~ A + B + C, data = X), then I will get a p-value for "A" (for example). If
the p-value is very small, I conclude that levels of "A" differ as a whole
regarding response. 

Now, suppose "A" has 3 levels 1, 2 and 3. I would like to assess the 3
differences between 1 and 2, 1 and 3, 2 and 3. 

My question is just : how do I have to modify the code inside lm( ) [or
outside lm( ), by adding specific instructions] to get an ouput giving me
the 3 p-values for the 3 differences. 

Maybe the answer is obvious to some of you, but I really not know exactly
what instructions / code do I have to use to get properly these p-values.

