Andre,

One of many ways to do this:

library(Hmisc,T); library(Design,T)
f <- ols(R ~ A + B + C, data=X)
contrast(f, list(A='1'), list(A=c('2','3')))
contrast(f, list(A='2'), list(A=c('1','3')))

Variables not mentioned in list( ) are set to reference values (mode).  This 
code works when interations are present too, but in that case you will often 
specify the levels of the interacting factors:
contrast(f, list(A='1',B='whatever'), list(A=c('2','3'),B='whatever'))
---- 
