Subject: matrix/array/table form into columnar form.
Message-ID: <3e026b72.160d7d.12272@imap.qut.edu.au>

Dear All,

One of the frequent thing we have to do in terms of data analysis is to
translate the matrix/array/table form of data into a columnar form.

For example suppose I have the following array:

junk<-array(c(1:8, 11:18, 111:118), dim = c(2,4,3)) 

# I will want to create this into columnar form which uses:

cbind(c(junk),rep(1:ncol(junk),dim(junk)[1]*dim(junk)[3]),rep(1:nrow(junk),dim(junk)[2]*dim(junk)[3])

# Will do what I want.

However, is this the only way? As it seems to be rather inefficient and is
there a command that will sort of collapse them down into columnar form?
The other question I have is to do with adding the matrices inside an
array, so how do I add the matrices in the junk array elegantly?

Thanks in advance.

Steve.

