References: <F5c1xuFhlGLjordHiNU00016b76@hotmail.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.31.0212280812360.7934-100000@gannet.stats>

TIF is hardly well-defined: it is a collection of formats of which most
tools only implement a subset.  Let's hope you have a simple version, with
just a header followed by the data.

ImageMagick's convert program (free from http://www.imagemagick.org) can
convert TIF to an ascii matrix.  There are other ways, e.g. netpbm.

R has a pixmap library that can read various formats to which ImageMagick
(and others) can convert, but I would convert to raw greylevels and read
via readBin().  Unfortunately S-PLUS can't read 16-bit integers directly
AFAIK.

